## Active Modules

| Module | Registered in `AppModule` | TypeORM |
|--------|---------------------------|---------|
| `DatabaseModule` | Yes (first) | `forRootAsync` via `buildTypeOrmConfig()` |
| `AuthModule` | Yes | `forFeature([User])` |
| `UserModule` | Yes | — (add `forFeature([User])` when implementing CRUD) |
| `CompanyModule` | Yes | — (add `forFeature([Company])` when implementing CRUD) |
| `MailModule` | Yes | — |

## TypeORM Pattern

- **Root connection**: `DatabaseModule` → `TypeOrmModule.forRootAsync` + `ConfigService`
- **Feature repos**: `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([Entity])` in each module that needs DB access
- **Injection**: `@InjectRepository(Entity)` — never use custom provider tokens
- **CLI**: `typeormFile.ts` reuses `buildTypeOrmConfig()` from `typeorm.config.ts`
- **Entities glob**: `src/**/*.entity.ts` (compiled to `dist/**/*.entity.js`)

## Auth

- Global `AuthGuard` registered via `APP_GUARD` in `AuthModule`
- JWT stored in `access_token` cookie (also accepts `Authorization` header)
- `@CurrentUser()` returns `UserSignature` (`id`, `name`, `role`, `companyIds`)
- `Role` enum lives in `src/common/role.enum.ts` — not in `auth/`

## Conventions

- **New feature**: create `src/<feature>/` with module, controller, service, entity; add `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([Entity])`; import in `app.module.ts`
- **Shared enums/types**: place in `src/common/`
- **Module order in `AppModule`**: `DatabaseModule` must load before modules that use TypeORM
- **Env config**: global `ConfigModule` reads `./.env.${process.env.NODE_ENV}`
- **Do not edit**: `dist/`, `node_modules/`, `infra/postgres_data/`

## Commands

```bash
npm run start:dev                                              # Dev server
docker compose up                                              # App :8090, Postgres :55432
npm run build && npm run migration:generate src/database/migrations/<name>
npm run migration:run                                          # Apply migrations
npm run migration:show                                         # Migration status
npm run seed:run                                               # Run default seed
```
